{
  "_readme": [
    "Vocabulary for the EXIF query parser (natural-language photo search).",
    "Edit this file to teach the parser new words — no rebuild needed,",
    "changes apply on server restart. All entries must be lowercase;",
    "multi-word phrases are allowed and match across any whitespace.",
    "A list present here REPLACES the built-in default list wholesale;",
    "a list you delete falls back to the built-in defaults.",
    "The query GRAMMAR (shapes like 'iso above N', 'f/2.8', '1/500',",
    "4-digit years) is fixed in code — this file only supplies the words",
    "those patterns alternate over. Symbols are ordinary words here:",
    "'>' and '<=' sit in the comparison lists like 'above' and 'at most'.",
    "A comparator may be followed by an optional 'than', and the numeric",
    "dimensions accept a spelled-out name ('aperture', 'f-stop', 'focal",
    "length') in front of it. Path is configurable via the",
    "'search.keywordsPath' setting (default: config/exif_search_keywords.json).",
    "'settings' (PLACE-4): a category name users say ('waterfront', 'beach') -> the GeoNames feature codes a photo must be at/near; 'shoreline': true also accepts the Natural Earth distance-to-water."
  ],
